    "title": "Burkina Faso – Travel guide at Wikivoyage",
    "text": "| WARNING: Because of widespread civil unrest, terrorist attacks, crime and kidnappings, avoid all travel to Burkina Faso including the capital, Ouagadougou. | | Government travel advisories | | | (Information last updated 26 Aug 2025) | Burkina Faso is a landlocked country in West Africa. Burkina Faso is one of the friendliest countries in all of Africa. Until unrest began in the late 2010s that made travel to the country unsafe, it received only a few tourists per year, and was an excellent destination for anyone interested in seeing a beautiful West African country and exploring African culture and music. It offers a diverse traditional culture, history, tribal art and a variety of landscapes. Regions [edit]| Volta Delta The country's population center, home to the mostly Christian Mossi and the national capital. | | Black Volta Region The lushest and most culturally diverse section of the country. | |",
    "source_type": "web",
    "domain": "tourisme_burkina",
    "language": "fr",
    "chunk_idx": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "f9b844a9fc5ae6f7_chunk_1",
    "parent_id": "f9b844a9fc5ae6f7",
