  },
  {
    "id": "396ba367ecaf0138_chunk_17",
    "parent_id": "396ba367ecaf0138",
    "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Ouagadougou",
    "title": "Ouagadougou – Travel guide at Wikivoyage",
    "text": "+226 50311717. - 9 Sonia Hotels Ouagadougou, Secteur 6, Rue Mogho Naaba Kiba, Kamsonghin, ☏ +226 25334022. This is like a modern highrise rising up above the shanties. Restaurant, lounge, sparkling pool and patio, plus gym, spa, a/c, and wifi. Next to the airport. A classy place. ~CFA 65000. - 10 Princess Yenega, Avenue de la grande Chancellerie, Koulouba (couple blocks east of the music museum), ☏ +226 70216315. Hotel with Burkinese-style architecture and garden, named after the legendary goddess of the Mossi people. Pool and restaurant and bar. Nice downtown location. Kind of high priced though. Splurge [edit]- 11 Bravia Hotel Ouagadougou, Sector 4, District ZACA, ☏ +226 25333271. Pool, hot tub, gym, restaurant, bar, wifi, a/c. Multi-story property that is ridiculously priced, but you can look over the squalor beneath you. ~CFA 105815. Connect [edit]Post Office: - Grande Post (Sonapost) downtown, right on the Place des Nations Unies",
